     These macros operate on strings of bits.

     The function bbiitt__aalllloocc() returns a pointer of type “_b_i_t_s_t_r___t _*” to suffi‐
     cient space to store _n_b_i_t_s bits, or NULL if no space is available.  If
     successful, the returned bit string is initialized with all bits cleared.

     The macro bbiitt__ddeeccll() declares a bit string with sufficient space to store
     _n_b_i_t_s bits.  bbiitt__ddeeccll() may be used to include statically sized bit
     strings in structure definitions or to create bit strings on the stack.
     Users of this macro are responsible for initialization of the bit string,
     typically via a global initialization of the containing struct or use of
     the bbiitt__nnsseett() or bbiinn__nncclleeaarr() functions.

     The macro bbiittssttrr__ssiizzee() returns the number of bytes necessary to store
     _n_b_i_t_s bits.  This is useful for copying bit strings.

     The functions bbiitt__cclleeaarr() and bbiitt__sseett() clear or set the zero-based num‐
     bered bit _b_i_t, in the bit string _n_a_m_e.

     The bbiitt__nnsseett() and bbiitt__nncclleeaarr() functions set or clear the zero-based
     numbered bits from _s_t_a_r_t through _s_t_o_p in the bit string _n_a_m_e.

     The bbiitt__tteesstt() function evaluates to non-zero if the zero-based numbered
     bit _b_i_t of bit string _n_a_m_e is set, and zero otherwise.

     The bbiitt__nntteesstt() function evaluates to non-zero if the zero-based numbered
     bits from _s_t_a_r_t through _s_t_o_p in the bit string _n_a_m_e all have the value
     _m_a_t_c_h.

     The function bbiitt__ffffcc() stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     zero-based number of the first bit not set in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits
     referenced by _n_a_m_e.  If all bits are set, the location referenced by
     _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffss() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     zero-based number of the first bit set in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits refer‐
     enced by _n_a_m_e.  If no bits are set, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is
     set to -1.

     The function bbiitt__ffffcc__aatt() stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     zero-based number of the first bit not set in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits
     referenced by _n_a_m_e, at or after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t.  If all
     bits at or after _s_t_a_r_t are set, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set
     to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffss__aatt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     zero-based number of the first bit set in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits refer‐
     enced by _n_a_m_e, at or after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t.  If no bits
     are set after _s_t_a_r_t, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffff__aatt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     zero-based number of the first bit in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced
     by _n_a_m_e, at or after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t that has value _m_a_t_c_h.
     If no bits after _s_t_a_r_t match that value, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffcc__aarreeaa() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     the zero-based number of the first bit beginning a sequence of unset bits
     of at least _s_i_z_e unset bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by
     _n_a_m_e.  If no sequence of contiguous unset bits of the specified _s_i_z_e can
     be found, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffss__aarreeaa() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     the zero-based number of the first bit beginning a sequence of set bits
     of at least _s_i_z_e set bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by _n_a_m_e.
     If no sequence of contiguous set bits of the specified _s_i_z_e can be found,
     the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffcc__aarreeaa__aatt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     the zero-based number of the first bit beginning a sequence of unset bits
     of at least _s_i_z_e unset bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by
     _n_a_m_e, at or after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t.  If no sequence of con‐
     tiguous unset bits of the specified _s_i_z_e can be found at or after _s_t_a_r_t,
     the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffffss__aarreeaa__aatt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     the zero-based number of the first bit beginning a sequence of set bits
     of at least _s_i_z_e set bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by _n_a_m_e,
     at or after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t.  If no sequence of contiguous
     set bits of the specified _s_i_z_e can be found at or after _s_t_a_r_t, the loca‐
     tion referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to -1.

     The bbiitt__ffff__aarreeaa__aatt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e
     the zero-based number of the first bit beginning a sequence of bits of at
     least _s_i_z_e bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by _n_a_m_e, at or af‐
     ter the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t in which all bits have the value
     _m_a_t_c_h.  If no sequence of contiguous such bits of the specified _s_i_z_e can
     be found at or after _s_t_a_r_t, the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e is set to
     -1.

     The bbiitt__ccoouunntt() function stores in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e the
     number of bits set in the array of _n_b_i_t_s bits referenced by _n_a_m_e, at or
     after the zero-based bit index _s_t_a_r_t.

     The macro bbiitt__ffoorreeaacchh() traverses all set bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s ref‐
     erenced by _n_a_m_e in the forward direction, assigning each location in turn
     to _v_a_r.

     The macro bbiitt__ffoorreeaacchh__aatt() traverses all set bits in the array of _n_b_i_t_s
     referenced by _n_a_m_e in the forward direction at or after the zero-based
     bit index _s_t_a_r_t, assigning each location in turn to _v_a_r.

     The macro bbiitt__ffoorreeaacchh__uunnsseett() traverses all unset bits in the array of
     _n_b_i_t_s referenced by _n_a_m_e in the forward direction, assigning each loca‐
     tion in turn to _v_a_r.

     The macro bbiitt__ffoorreeaacchh__uunnsseett__aatt() traverses all unset bits in the array of
     _n_b_i_t_s referenced by _n_a_m_e in the forward direction at or after the zero-
     based bit index _s_t_a_r_t, assigning each location in turn to _v_a_r.

     The arguments in bit string macros are evaluated only once and may safely
     have side effects.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
           #include <limits.h>
           #include <bitstring.h>

           ...
           #define LPR_BUSY_BIT            0
           #define LPR_FORMAT_BIT          1
           #define LPR_DOWNLOAD_BIT        2
           ...
           #define LPR_AVAILABLE_BIT       9
           #define LPR_MAX_BITS            10

           make_lpr_available()
           {
                   bitstr_t bit_decl(bitlist, LPR_MAX_BITS);
                   ...
                   bit_nclear(bitlist, 0, LPR_MAX_BITS - 1);
                   ...
                   if (!bit_test(bitlist, LPR_BUSY_BIT)) {
                           bit_clear(bitlist, LPR_FORMAT_BIT);
                           bit_clear(bitlist, LPR_DOWNLOAD_BIT);
                           bit_set(bitlist, LPR_AVAILABLE_BIT);
                   }
           }

